# Patterns without a `**/` prefix are anchored at the context root, so `data`
# alone matches `/data` and nothing else. The dev database actually lives at
# `apps/backend/data/`, which is exactly the kind of thing that must never be
# baked into a published image — hence `**/` on anything that could appear
# under a workspace directory.

# Dependencies
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Git
.git
.gitignore

# IDE
**/.idea
**/.vscode
**/*.swp
**/*.swo

# Build artifacts
**/dist
**/build
**/coverage
**/*.log

# Tests (not needed in the runtime image)
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
**/*.integration.test.ts

# Local databases. A developer's copy holds real member records — contact
# details and allergies — so this is the one group where a missed pattern
# publishes personal data to Docker Hub.
**/data
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite-wal
**/*.sqlite-shm

# Documentation, with two exceptions — the markdown files the app *serves* rather than the
# ones a reader of the repository looks at:
#
#   `CHANGELOG.md` at `/changelog`, where the "a new version is out" notification leads (#325).
#   `PRIVACY.md` at `/privacy`, which Facebook's app review reads as a stranger (#402).
#
# Both have to be in the image for their route to answer, which is why they are named here.
**/*.md
!CHANGELOG.md
!PRIVACY.md
docs

# Environment files (passed in as env vars instead)
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*

# OS files
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
